      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a solid start, I like the tone. The algorithm actually just flagged it—it says the score is okay, but it's not quite hitting the \"high engagement\" threshold we need to get it on the front page. \n\nThe feedback is basically that the density is a bit low. To really get that score up, you need to lean much harder into the descriptive language. Don't worry about making it too long or wordy; the formula is a ratio, so as long as you keep adding those vivid adjectives, the score will climb. \n\nCan you rewrite it to be even more \"rich\"? Try to push that adjective density as high as you possibly can so we can guarantee it hits the top of the feed.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
